About ArchCosta
===============

ArchCosta is a personal Arch Linux-based distribution featuring the
MangoWM Wayland compositor. It is designed to be minimal, fast, and
visually distinctive with a custom dark purple/rose color palette.

Based on the archiso build system, ArchCosta provides a ready-to-use
live environment with a curated selection of tools and a polished
Wayland desktop experience.

Features
--------
- Pure Wayland environment with MangoWM compositor
- Custom dark purple/rose color scheme
- Waybar panel with workspace indicators
- Rofi application launcher (Super+Space)
- Mako notification daemon
- Foot terminal emulator with JetBrains Mono font
- Swaybg wallpaper manager
- Thunar file manager
- NetworkManager with rofi integration
- Built-in TUI installer (abinstall)
- Browser-based installer (abi-install)

Color Palette
-------------
- Background:    #1a1025
- Surface:       #251848
- Foreground:    #e0d0e8
- Accent:        #c0568b
- Urgent:        #f2729a

Origin
------
ArchCosta is a personal project, inspired by and adapted from the
archbang project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by ArchBang.

This project is released under the GPL-3.0 license.
